# ALTAI VS Code engineering rules

- Read `docs/ENGINEERING_PLAN.md` before planning or making code changes.
- Treat `altaidevorg/altai-app` as the owner of shared UI, host contracts,
  protocol packages, and the Rust agent service.
- Treat this repository as a thin VS Code host and adapter.
- Never copy ALTAI Desktop JSX, CSS, stores, or protocol definitions into this
  repository. Consume versioned shared packages instead.
- Never implement a second chat interface. The Webview must render
  `@altai/agent-ui`.
- Keep `vscode` imports in Extension Host adapter code. Webview code communicates
  through typed, runtime-validated messages.
- Keep provider credentials, IsanAgent, shell, MCP, and durable storage behind
  the Rust host. Never expose secrets to the Webview.
- Do not start the native host for an untrusted workspace.
- Gate visible controls using negotiated host capabilities. Do not ship enabled
  placeholders or dead buttons.
- Keep changes small enough for one reviewable pull request and one acceptance
  gate from the engineering plan.
- Add or update tests with every behavior change.
- Before finishing, run the relevant typecheck, lint, test, and build commands.
- Report changed files, verification commands and results, compatibility impact,
  and remaining risks.
